From 405d3e9821d119185265d9bdd16e770bc3393d5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher AMIAUD <christopher.amiaud@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:20:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Track the host fd behind each guest fd

Each Fd now records the host fd it wraps, and every host call goes
through it, instead of assuming the guest number is the host's.

By default the two numbers stay equal and nothing changes. Defining
HAVE_VIRTUAL_FDS makes blink choose the guest numbers itself (lowest
free one, like Linux) and implement the dup family on top of a host
dup(). That's needed when guest processes share a single host fd
table, which is the case when fork() is emulated with threads.

The mode can be tested on any host: add HAVE_VIRTUAL_FDS to config.h
and run `make check` with some host fds held open, so host and guest
numbers diverge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
